{
	"sources": {
		"project-all-documented": "https://docs.dokploy.com/docs/api, the example answer of GET /api/project.all, verbatim",
		"dokploy-v0.30.10": "https://github.com/Dokploy/dokploy/tree/v0.30.10: apps/dokploy/server/api/routers/project.ts (all, as an owner or admin), routers/application.ts (one; deploy, which returns nothing on a server of its own, so its 200 has no body; dropDeployment, which returns true), routers/deployment.ts (all), packages/server/src/services/application.ts (findApplicationById), services/deployment.ts (findAllDeploymentsByApplicationId), the tables of packages/server/src/db/schema/ (project, environment, application, domain, deployment, tag), and the error body of @dokploy/trpc-openapi 0.0.18 (adapters/node-http/core.js, with `issues` when zod refuses the input, and input.js, which parses JSON only under exactly application/json) with apps/dokploy/server/api/trpc.ts (errorFormatter, its flattened zodError) and pages/api/[...trpc].ts (the 401 without a key)",
		"dokploy-v0.30.10-setup": "https://github.com/Dokploy/dokploy/tree/v0.30.10: apps/dokploy/server/api/routers/application.ts (create, which returns the row it inserted; saveBuildType and saveEnvironment, which return true), routers/domain.ts (create, which returns the row; validateDomain), routers/mount.ts (create, which returns the row; mounted as mounts in api/root.ts), packages/server/src/services/domain.ts (validateDomain: { isValid, resolvedIp } when the host resolves to the server, with error when it does not, { isValid, error } when it does not resolve), and the tables of packages/server/src/db/schema/ (application, domain, mount)",
		"dokploy-v0.30.10-source": "https://github.com/Dokploy/dokploy/tree/v0.30.10: apps/dokploy/server/api/routers/github.ts (githubProviders: each { githubId, githubUrl, gitProvider } with every column of the git_provider table; getGithubRepositories and getGithubBranches, which answer octokit.paginate's list of GitHub's own repositories and branches: github-examples.json), routers/application.ts (saveGithubProvider and update, which return true), packages/server/src/services/application.ts (findApplicationById: github without githubClientSecret, githubPrivateKey and githubWebhookSecret), and the tables of packages/server/src/db/schema/ (github, git-provider)"
	},
	"recorded": "2026-10-31, the writes (application-drop-deployment, error-input) 2026-11-06; the setup writes (application-create, application-save-build-type, application-save-environment, domain-create, mounts-create, domain-validate-domain*) and application-one.mounts 2026-11-06; the source routes (github-*, application-save-github-provider, application-update) and application-one.github 2026-11-10",
	"how": "the keys of each answer at every depth; a list holds its first item's keys, any other value null. Dokploy's openapi.json gives {} for every 200, so the shapes come from the documentation's one example (project-all-documented) and from the source at v0.30.10 (the rest). A related record findApplicationById reads that the fake answers empty or null (redirects, security, ports, previewDeployments; the git providers but github, server and registries) is [] or null here: not compared below. application.deploy answers no JSON at all, so it has no shape. GitHub's repositories and branches come from docs.github.com's examples (github-examples.json)",
